---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Privacy Blur for Slack"
  description="Privacy policy for Privacy Blur for Slack. Learn what stays local, what limited usage information is collected, and how your privacy is protected."
  canonical="https://amrita-labs.com/privacy-blur-slack/privacy/"
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 prose prose-invert prose-sm">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white">Privacy Policy — Privacy Blur for Slack</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400"><strong>Effective Date</strong>: 2026-07-19 · <strong>Last Updated</strong>: 2026-08-15</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">1. Who We Are</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">Privacy Blur for Slack is operated by Amrita Labs.<br />Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@amrita-labs.com" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">hello@amrita-labs.com</a></p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">2. What This Extension Does</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">Privacy Blur for Slack blurs sensitive content (messages, sender names, channel lists, and media) on Slack Web during screen sharing, video calls, and presentations. It operates entirely client-side within your browser.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">3. Data We Collect</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">We collect <strong>minimal</strong> data:</p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="text-sm text-gray-300 w-full">
        <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10"><th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Category</th><th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">What</th><th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Why</th><th class="text-left py-2">Retention</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4">User preferences</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Zone toggles, custom rules, trial timestamp</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Persist settings across sessions (Pro only)</td><td class="py-2">Stored in browser storage and, where enabled by Chrome, synced across your browsers</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Anonymous product analytics</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Random ID, event name and properties, extension version</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Understand feature use and detect reliability issues</td><td class="py-2">Sent to an analytics provider under its retention policy</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">Payment status</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Paid/unpaid flag from the payment provider</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Unlock Pro features</td><td class="py-2">Managed by the payment provider</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mt-4">We do <strong>NOT</strong> collect:</p>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>Slack message content — we cannot read your messages</li>
      <li>Sender names, channel names, or any text content</li>
      <li>Browsing history or page URLs</li>
      <li>Screenshots or screen recordings</li>
      <li>Any personally identifiable information</li>
      <li>Slack message content, workspace details, or browsing activity in analytics</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">4. What Leaves Your Browser</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300"><strong>Slack content stays local.</strong> The extension operates client-side. Its external communication is limited to:</p>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li><strong>Anonymous product analytics</strong>: An analytics provider receives a random ID, event name and properties, and extension version. This never includes Slack message content, names, workspace details, URLs, or browsing history.</li>
      <li><strong>Payment processing</strong>: When you choose to upgrade, a payment provider handles payment-related details. We do not see your full card number.</li>
      <li><strong>Browser sync</strong>: If enabled by your browser, your preferences may sync across your browsers through the browser's built-in sync feature.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mt-4">No Slack data or message content is transmitted to our analytics, payment, or service providers.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">5. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="text-sm text-gray-300 w-full">
        <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10"><th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Service</th><th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Data shared</th><th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Purpose</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Payment providers</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Email (if provided), payment info</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Subscription billing</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Analytics providers</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Random ID, anonymous product events, extension version</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Product analytics and reliability monitoring</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">Browser sync providers</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Extension preferences when sync is enabled</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Settings persistence across devices</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mt-4">We do not use advertising networks or data brokers. We do <strong>NOT</strong> sell, share, or rent your data.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">6. Your Rights</h2>
    <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-white mt-6">GDPR (EU users)</h3>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>Right to access, rectify, erase, restrict, or port your data</li>
      <li>Right to object to processing</li>
      <li>Right to lodge a complaint with your supervisory authority</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-white mt-6">CCPA / CPRA (California users)</h3>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>Right to know what we collect</li>
      <li>Right to delete</li>
      <li>Right to opt out of "sale" or "sharing" — we do not sell or share your data</li>
      <li>Right to non-discrimination</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-white mt-6">PIPEDA (Canadian users)</h3>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>Right to know what personal information we hold and how it is used</li>
      <li>Right to access and challenge accuracy</li>
      <li>Right to withdraw consent at any time</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mt-4">For any rights request: <a href="mailto:hello@amrita-labs.com" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">hello@amrita-labs.com</a></p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">7. Data Retention & Deletion</h2>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>Preferences: stored in browser storage and deleted when you uninstall the extension or clear extension data</li>
      <li>Anonymous analytics events: retained only as reasonably necessary for product improvement and reliability</li>
      <li>Payment records: retained by payment providers under their applicable policies</li>
      <li>We retain no Slack content or server-side profile about you</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mt-4">To delete all data: uninstall the extension. All local data is immediately removed.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">8. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">This extension is not intended for users under 13 (COPPA) or under 16 in the EU (GDPR). We do not knowingly collect data from children.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">9. Security</h2>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>Slack content remains client-side; only limited anonymous usage information is sent as described above</li>
      <li>Payment details are handled by payment providers</li>
      <li>Reasonable technical and organizational safeguards are used to protect information</li>
      <li>Content script only runs on *.slack.com — no access to other sites</li>
      <li>Extension code is open for inspection (no obfuscation)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">We may update this policy at any time. Material changes will be communicated via the extension's update notes and by updating the "Last Updated" date above. Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">11. Contact</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">For any privacy questions: <a href="mailto:hello@amrita-labs.com" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">hello@amrita-labs.com</a></p>
  </article>

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pb-12 flex gap-6 text-xs text-gray-500">
    <a href="/privacy-blur-slack/" class="hover:text-gray-400">← Back to Privacy Blur for Slack</a>
  </div>
</Base>
